e7 wire log v1
device   GS Music e7, serial 361, USB, driven from Node over CoreMIDI
input    GS-e7 Analog Synthesizer
output   GS-e7 Analog Synthesizer
date     2026-08-22
session  Turning LfoClockRate's knob against the display to fix its zone boundaries

# LfoClockRate: which musical division the display showed at each controller value.
# The instrument's display answers only to the panel, never to an incoming CC, so this
# was captured the other way round: a person turned the knob and the bench read the
# value back. Byte 54 carries it, and tracks CC 76 exactly, so the inbound CC
# run below is the same measurement a second time rather than separate evidence. The
# divisions themselves appear in no frame here — they were read off the OLED by eye.
# LFO 1 Mode = Clock Sync was set over CC 60, and a 24 PPQN clock at 120 BPM ran
# throughout, sent unlogged so it could not bury the capture.
# 
#   up-sweep marks (division appeared at):
#       0   Whole Note
#       8   Dotted 1/2 Note
#      16   Whole Note Triplet
#      24   1/2 Note
#      32   Dotted 1/4 Note
#      40   1/2 Note Triplet
#      48   1/4 Note
#      56   Dotted 1/8 Note
#      64   1/4 Note Triplet
#      72   1/8 Note
#      80   Dotted 1/16 Note
#      88   1/8 Note Triplet
#      96   1/16 Note
#     104   1/16 Note Triplet
#     112   1/32 Note
# 
#   down-sweep marks (division appeared at):
#     127   1/32 Note
#     111   1/16 Note Triplet
#     103   1/16 Note
#      95   1/8 Note Triplet
#      87   Dotted 1/16 Note
#      79   1/8 Note
#      71   1/4 Note Triplet
#      63   Dotted 1/8 Note
#      55   1/4 Note
#      46   1/2 Note Triplet
#      39   Dotted 1/4 Note
#      31   1/2 Note
#      23   Whole Note Triplet
#      15   Dotted 1/2 Note
#       7   Whole Note
# 
#   zones, after closing the brackets:
#       0-7   Whole Note
#       8-15  Dotted 1/2 Note
#      16-23  Whole Note Triplet
#      24-31  1/2 Note
#      32-39  Dotted 1/4 Note
#      40-47  1/2 Note Triplet
#      48-55  1/4 Note
#      56-63  Dotted 1/8 Note
#      64-71  1/4 Note Triplet
#      72-79  1/8 Note
#      80-87  Dotted 1/16 Note
#      88-95  1/8 Note Triplet
#      96-103 1/16 Note
#     104-111 1/16 Note Triplet
#     112-127 1/32 Note
